=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
  play firewall ------------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's own screens and prompts, on the real$
# plan/apply engine against a simulated host, hostfake's$
# recording host.System, whose commands a model of the host$
# answers. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's, and its record is shown when play ends.$
$
# Firewall hosts ###############################################$
$
  Select a host$
$
   1) Debian 13            No ufw$
   2) Ubuntu 26.04         ufw inactive, ssh.socket$
   3) Active on 22         Deny policy, SSH let through$
   4) Hardened             Deny policy, sshd on 2230$
   5) Allow policy         ufw on, refusing nothing$
   6) Lockout              ufw refuses SSH$
   7) Lockout at start     Stopped, saved rules refuse SSH$
   8) Allowlist            SSH from some sources$
   9) Blocklist            A saved deny before the allow$
  10) Edit not reloaded    Configured 2230, sshd on 22$
  11) Bound elsewhere      Configured 22, sshd on 2230$
  12) Denied               ufw denies 22$
  13) Alpine 3.24          No ufw$
  14) Alpine 3.23, stock   No ufw, no ss, no index$
  15) Alpine, no runlevel  Active, gone after a reboot$
  16) Service off          Active, gone after a reboot$
  17) Proxmox VE 9         pve-firewall disabled$
  18) Proxmox VE 9, drop   pve-firewall on, DROP$
  19) Proxmox VE 9, ufw on ufw left on$
  20) Two profiles         hardn.yml has two$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter your choice [0-20 or q]: 3$
$
# Info: firewall/active22$
# web-01.example.net runs Debian 13. ufw active, default deny$
# incoming, allowing 22, where sshd listens.$
$
# UFW Firewall Configuration ###################################$
$
  [+] Firewall             Configured deny policy$
$
  ufw ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Installed            Yes$
  [+] Status               Active$
  [+] Incoming policy      Deny$
  [+] At boot              Yes$
$
  SSH ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] [::]:22              Allowed$
  [+] 0.0.0.0:22           Allowed$
$
  Rules --------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] 22/tcp               Allow$
  [+] 22/tcp (v6)          Allow$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Disable firewall     Stop ufw (not recommended)$
   2) Application Profiles Add, remove, apply$
   3) Trusted Interfaces   Add, remove, apply$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter selection [0-3 or q]: 0$
$
# Firewall hosts ###############################################$
$
  Select a host$
$
   1) Debian 13            No ufw$
   2) Ubuntu 26.04         ufw inactive, ssh.socket$
   3) Active on 22         Deny policy, SSH let through$
   4) Hardened             Deny policy, sshd on 2230$
   5) Allow policy         ufw on, refusing nothing$
